# Domain safety

Protect accepted ranch semantics. Do not create new ranch rules in this file.

Read the relevant documents under [docs/domain/](../../docs/domain/README.md) and the [open-question registry](../../docs/domain/open-questions.md). Follow [docs/product/uncertainty-protocol.md](../../docs/product/uncertainty-protocol.md). Current ranch facts live in the domain documents. The desired model in [docs/maps/to-be/](../../docs/maps/to-be/README.md) is not current practice and is not approved product scope. Do not replace those sources with generic livestock practice.

- Never replace a ranch fact with a generic livestock assumption.
- Unknown remains a valid state.
- Keep declared, observed, measured, and inferred distinct. Evidence does not upgrade source quality by itself.
- An inference is not a confirmation. One known bull does not confirm paternity.
- A correction of a mistaken value is not the same thing as a later real-world event.
- One fact has one authoritative owner. Derived information does not write that fact.
- Leave a domain question open until it is explicitly resolved and recorded.
- A future hardware capability is not current domain behavior.

Keep `a la parte` and `bulto` in their original terms. Neither is a settled settlement rule or a price per head. `SINIIGA` names the official ear tag. It is not an integration design.

If the task needs a missing ranch fact, stop and ask. Do not invent it.
